{#
    The page a route shows when the editor may not read what they asked for (ADR 0019).

    IT EXTENDS THE LAYOUT ON PURPOSE. The editor is signed in and the layout works, so this is
    a page of the admin and not a failure of it — unlike `GuardsCoreVersion::refusal()`, which
    renders without Twig because the setup the layout depends on is what broke there.

    THE MENU COMES ALONG, and it now lists only readable entities. A refusal that also shows
    where the editor *may* go is a refusal rather than a dead end.
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="admin"{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="admin__main admin-refused">
    <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
    <p class="admin-refused__message" role="status">{{ message }}</p>
</main>
{% endblock %}
